88:     * A figure with the claim's late charge on top: the late percent in force on the claim's date of the figure for every
89-     * full 30 days an OPEN or PENDING claim is past its due-by (fixed when it was added) on the sheet's
90-     * today, rounded by the claim's date against the policy date. The charge is never bound: it always follows the sheet's today.
--
118:     * A claim's amount at the rate the grade has in force on the claim's date, raised to the floor in
119-     * force on the claim's date when below it (a correction has no floor), rounded by the claim's date against the policy
120-     * date; null when it has no rate.
     * Add a claim for a person on the sheet; with no date it is dated the sheet's today. Refused when
     * it is dated inside a closed period, or when it is a correction that does not name a SETTLED claim
     * of the same person (see {@link #refuseUnlessCorrects}).
     */
    @Transactional
    public Claim add(String sheetId, String user, long personId, BigDecimal amount, LocalDate date, String note,
            String corrects) {
        Rollups.Rollup before = rollups.take(sheetId);
        Person person = person(sheetId, personId);
        LocalDate dated = date != null ? date : sheets.today(sheetId);
        LocalDate dueBy = dated.plusDays(sheets.lock(sheetId).termsFor(person.gradeOn(dated), dated));
        periods.refuseIfClosed(sheetId, dated);

